\[
\mathcal{H}
=
\text{finite-core geometric history with transported internal structure}.
\]

The history may be represented by a spine \(X(s,\tau)\), a moving frame \(F(s,\tau)\), a cross-section or thickness, and possibly discrete topological data. Particle identity would then be a stable equivalence class or attractor of this geometric system rather than a label inserted into the action.

This is the correct direction for a generative theory.

