# 2. Current conceptual architecture

## Core primitive: framed finite-core history

The most stable provisional state is:

\[
\mathcal G(s,\tau)=
\left(
X,F,A,\chi,q,\mathcal C,\mathcal B
\right).
\]

- \(X(s,\tau)\in\mathbb R^4\): material spine/history.
- \(F(s,\tau)\in SO(4)\): transported orthonormal frame.
- \(A\): finite-core cross-section or tube data.
- \(\chi\): internal phase.
- \(q\): optional topology or assembly state.
- \(\mathcal C\): constraints.
- \(\mathcal B\): boundary and closure conditions.

The key architectural shift is:

\[
\text{particle}
\neq
\text{primitive label},
\]

but potentially

\[
\text{particle-like identity}
=
\text{stable solution/topology/readout class of }\mathcal G.
\]

## Minimal mechanics

The current baseline action is:

\[
S[X_a]
=
\sum_a\int d\tau\,ds
\left[
\frac{\rho_a}{2}|\partial_\tau X_a|^2
-\frac{T_a}{2}|\partial_s X_a|^2
-\frac{\kappa_a}{2}|\partial_s^2 X_a|^2
-U_a(X_a)
\right]
+S_{\mathrm{int}}.
\]

This is not the final SAT action. It is the smallest mechanical kernel currently capable of supporting:

- equilibrium;
- Euler–Lagrange equations;
- Hessians;
- wave propagation;
- bending;
- stability;
- interactions;
- coarse-graining.

The rebuild’s strongest current policy is: **do not add a term because it has a desirable interpretation. Add it only when its object, dimensions, symmetry, and constitutive origin are defined.**

## Parameter grammar

The current core distinction should remain:

\[
s=\text{material/arclength coordinate},
\]

\[
\tau=\text{microscopic evolution variable},
\]

\[
t=\text{observed time only after readout},
\]

\[
\lambda=\text{auxiliary generator or affine parameter when separately defined},
\]

\[
r=\text{radial/scale variable}.
\]

Conflating these variables was one of the largest defects in the inherited architecture.

