U_a(X_a)
\right]
+
S_{\mathrm{int}}.
\]

This supplies interfaces for:

- evolution inertia;
- first-gradient response;
- bending;
- constitutive potential;
- interaction.

It should not be called the final SAT Lagrangian.

The interaction sector should remain decomposed:

\[
S_{\mathrm{int}}
=
S_{\mathrm{contact}}
+
S_{\mathrm{excluded}}
+
S_{\mathrm{local}}
+
S_{\mathrm{nonlocal}}
+
S_{\mathrm{topological}}
+
S_{\mathrm{mediated}}.
\]

That prevents “Interbraid” from becoming an undefined bucket containing physically distinct mechanisms.

