## Scrollsaw

Scrollsaw should be the **equation-to-geometry compiler and rewriting calculus**.

This is the most important new design.

Its job is not merely to visualize equations. It should translate mathematical operators into an intermediate geometric language.

For example:

| Mathematical object | Scrollsaw geometric operation |
|---|---|
| \(\partial_sX\) | oriented tangent transport |
| \(\partial_s^2X\) | bending operator |
| \(\partial_\tau X\) | history evolution |
| \(\Omega=F'F^{-1}\) | local frame-rotation token |
| \(\int ds\) | composition along a strand |
| \(\sum_a\) | disjoint or interacting strand bundle |
| \(V_{ab}\) | connector/kernel between strands |
| constraint multiplier | clamp, guide surface, or closure gate |
| Hessian | local response block |
| determinantank collapse | carrier loss or bifurcation event |
| trace | internal-loop contraction |
| push-forward | hidden-structure eliminationeadout |
| variation \(\delta S=0\) | local rewrite balance condition |

This intermediate representation would let H(s)H borrow from:

- string diagrams;
- tensor networks;
- operads;
- knot and tangle categories;
- bond graphs;
- factor graphs;
- finite-element assembly graphs;
- automatic differentiation graphs;
- BV Feynman-graph expansions;
- geometric mechanics.

The goal should not be to reproduce BV terminology decoratively. It should reproduce the **computational operation** of eliminating internal degrees of freedom while preserving an effective boundary object.

## Proposed Scrollsaw pipeline

\[
\text{source equation}
\ightarrow
\text{typed operator graph}
\ightarrow
\text{geometric rewrite graph}
\ightarrow
\text{nested framed structure}
\ightarrow
\text{solver}
\ightarrow
\text{readout}
\ightarrow
\text{back-translation}.
\]

Every translation must preserve:

- dimensions;
- free and bound indices;
- differentiation variable;
- variational role;
- locality/nonlocality;
- boundary data;
- provenance;
- epistemic status.

This is the best place to exploit existing systems rather than inventing everything from zero.

